    "sp_qa": {
      "type": "sensol-product-qa",
      "blocks": {
        "qa_1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between the RS03 and the RS03 PRO?",
            "answer": "Both models share the same 500W servo motor system, 45 kg maximum resistance, 1 kg precision, 0–145° arm range, and chassis. The RS03 PRO's defining upgrade is its enhanced Pilates cable system, which provides smoother transitions, greater range of motion, more advanced sequencing capability, and a studio-grade tactile quality. The price difference is $400 AUD ($2,400 for RS03 vs $2,800 for RS03 PRO)."
          }
        },
        "qa_2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes the enhanced cables better than standard cables?",
            "answer": "The enhanced Pilates cables in the RS03 PRO are constructed from premium-grade materials with reinforced end fittings and a redesigned routing architecture. This results in: reduced friction through the cable path, greater effective range of motion (especially during rotational and lateral movements), more consistent tension throughout complex sequences, and better tactile responsiveness. Experienced Pilates practitioners will notice the difference immediately."
          }
        },
        "qa_3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the RS03 PRO worth the extra $400 over the RS03?",
            "answer": "If you are a dedicated Pilates practitioner, certified instructor, or use the reformer for professional purposes, the enhanced cables are a meaningful upgrade that you will feel in every session. If you are primarily interested in strength training, the RS03 may be sufficient. We recommend the PRO for anyone who trains four or more times per week or who has experience with studio-grade equipment."
          }
        },
        "qa_4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use the RS03 PRO professionally in a studio or clinic?",
            "answer": "Yes. The RS03 PRO is suitable for professional use in Pilates studios, physiotherapy practices, and personal training facilities. The enhanced cables, 500W motor, and AI-driven app are designed to meet the demands of professional practitioners. The Lifetime Warranty covers professional use. Many of our early adopters are certified instructors who use the RS03 PRO as their primary teaching tool."
          }
        },
        "qa_5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need a monthly subscription for the app?",
            "answer": "No. The Vesta Sensol App is completely free with no monthly fees, no locked content, and no usage limits. All 300+ guided classes, AI-driven coaching, progress tracking, and firmware updates are included with your purchase. This saves you $408–$480 per year compared to NordicTrack's iFIT ($34/month) or Frame Fitness ($39.99/month)."
          }
        },
        "qa_6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the warranty and return policy?",
            "answer": "The RS03 PRO comes with a Lifetime Warranty covering all manufacturing defects in materials and workmanship, including the enhanced cable system. We also offer a 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee — if you are not completely satisfied, return the RS03 PRO within 30 days for a full refund. Free domestic shipping is included to all Australian addresses."
          }
        },
        "qa_7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the RS03 PRO compare to the Technogym Reform ($15,650 AUD)?",
            "answer": "The Technogym Reform is a luxury product with a solid wood frame and vegan leather. However, it uses spring resistance — no digital weight, no adjustable arms, no training modes, and no AI coaching. The RS03 PRO offers all of these technologies at less than one-fifth of the price. If you prioritise training technology and performance, the RS03 PRO is the superior choice."
          }
        },
        "qa_8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How quickly will the RS03 PRO pay for itself?",
            "answer": "At $2,800 AUD compared to a $220/month unlimited studio membership, the RS03 PRO pays for itself in approximately 13 months. Compared to casual classes at $42.50/session (twice weekly), the break-even is approximately 8 months. Compared to private sessions at $120/session, the break-even is approximately 3 months. Over five years, the RS03 PRO delivers savings of $10,400–$16,400."
          }
        },
        "qa_9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What support is available in Australia?",
            "answer": "The RS03 PRO is distributed by Dute Fitness (Australia) Pty. Ltd. (ACN 700 632 337) with local stock and local support. Contact our Australian team at support@sensolfitness.com.au for any assistance. The Lifetime Warranty is honoured locally — no need to ship internationally for warranty service. Australian-plug power cords are included with every unit."
          }
        },
        "qa_10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the RS03 PRO compare to studio reformers?",
            "answer": "The RS03 PRO was specifically designed to deliver a studio-grade experience at home. The enhanced cables match the smoothness and responsiveness of professional studio equipment. The digital weight system actually exceeds what studio reformers offer — no studio reformer provides 1 kg precision, three training modes, or AI-driven coaching. The RS03 PRO's 56 kg weight and 13 cm ground clearance provide a comparably stable platform."
          }
        }
      },
